1. DEFINITIONS
--------------
"Software" means the NEURAL AURORA source code, binaries, assets, designs,
documentation, configuration, data models, APIs, and related materials.

"Licensor" means Amit Kumar (Techhackontime999), the copyright holder, or an
authorized successor/assignee.

"Commercial Use" includes any use intended for or resulting in direct or
indirect commercial advantage, monetary compensation, business operations,
client work, agency work, SaaS/hosted service, internal business deployment,
paid distribution, or embedding in a commercial offering.

"Approved Contributor" means a person who has applied, been evaluated, and been
explicitly approved by an authorized administrator, with approval recorded in
the project's official records/systems. A pull request, commit, issue, GitHub
account, star, fork, registration, or repository visibility does not by itself
create Approved Contributor status or grant any license.

"APPROVED_CONTRIBUTOR_PERSONAL License" means a limited, revocable,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable, personal-use-only license grant issued
after explicit admin approval and recorded issuance.

2. DEFAULT: PROPRIETARY / ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
---------------------------------------------
Except for rights preserved under Section "IMPORTANT LEGACY RIGHTS
PRESERVATION" or rights expressly granted in a separate written agreement signed
or otherwise formally issued by the Licensor, the Software is proprietary. No
license is granted by default.

You may not copy, modify, distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lease,
host, provide as a service, create derivative works for external use, or use the
Software for Commercial Use without an applicable written commercial license.

3. EVALUATION AND CONTRIBUTION SUBMISSIONS
------------------------------------------
Unless otherwise agreed in writing, viewing a public repository for evaluation
or submitting a contribution proposal/patch does not grant commercial rights.
Contributions may be accepted only under terms explicitly approved by the
Licensor. The Licensor may require a Contributor License Agreement (CLA), DCO,
or other written terms before accepting contributions.

4. APPROVED CONTRIBUTOR PERSONAL-USE PROGRAM (DRAFT POLICY)
-----------------------------------------------------------
The Licensor may, at sole discretion, operate an Approved Contributor
personal-use program. Eligibility requires:

  a. Submission of an application through the official channel.
  b. Evaluation of contribution/value by authorized maintainers/admins.
  c. Explicit admin approval recorded in an auditable system.
  d. Explicit license issuance recorded in an auditable system.

APPROVED_CONTRIBUTOR_PERSONAL grants, when issued, are limited to:

  - Personal, non-commercial use only.
  - Use by the named approved individual only.
  - Scope/term/product restrictions recorded in the grant.

APPROVED_CONTRIBUTOR_PERSONAL grants DO NOT include:

  - Organisation/company-wide use.
  - Commercial or client deployment.
  - SaaS/hosted service use for third parties.
  - Resale, redistribution, sublicensing, assignment, or transfer.
  - Paid/enterprise entitlements unless separately purchased.
  - Any transfer of copyright, patent, trademark, or other IP ownership.

The Licensor may suspend, revoke, or refuse renewal for misuse, policy
violation, security risk, fraud, legal risk, or non-payment where applicable.
Revocation does not create entitlement to refund except as required by law or
separate written agreement.

5. COMMERCIAL LICENSES
----------------------
Commercial use requires a valid commercial license or written agreement from the
Licensor. Pricing, scope, seats, term, deployment limits, support, and
enterprise entitlements are defined by the applicable commercial agreement/order.

6. NO IMPLIED RIGHTS / NO OWNERSHIP TRANSFER
--------------------------------------------
Except for expressly granted licenses, all rights, title, and interest in and
to the Software remain with the Licensor. No trademark rights are granted.
Contributors do not receive equity, employment, compensation, royalties, or IP
ownership by default unless explicitly agreed in a separate written agreement.

7. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
-------------------------
The Software may include or depend on third-party components under their own
licenses. Those third-party licenses remain applicable to those components. See
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` for a draft inventory; it requires review.

